35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"I found out that the prefecture rate sheet for publicly run beds is 1,100 yen per night per student bed, including hall and equipment use. The accounts from two clubs that went inland reported that they got their booked hall slots but had to sleep eight to a room with lights out at eleven. It seems like the inland option might be more affordable but less comfortable.","{""words"":67,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"I see. The vacation timetable for our own hall is already quite busy, and a continuous block would mean training split between early mornings and late evenings. Also, the campus canteen closes for the vacation block, and the club cooking for itself cost the duty pair two hours a day last year. Somewhere with kitchen staff would remove that burden.","{""words"":60,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"I found that group transport accounts for a significant portion of the budget, especially for trips further away. Whole-building lets at small inns have strict terms, with non-refundable deposits and fixed headcounts. This could be a problem if someone drops out late.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,"I found out that group bookings at publicly run centres go through a lottery six months ahead, and the nine-page application has to be resubmitted whole if a single date shifts. Also, the attendance sheets for the away camps show a fifth of the membership never came at all, and most of those names had gone from the register by winter. It seems like planning and ensuring everyone's attendance is crucial for a successful camp.","{""words"":75,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"I found that a third of the club cannot be on campus by nine in the morning without paying for a bed the night before. Also, the seniors who were asked all trace the year-groups actually mixing to the evenings after sessions, which only happen when everyone is sleeping in the same place. It seems like having everyone stay together might encourage better interaction and bonding.","{""words"":66,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shizue, that's interesting about our hall's timetable and the canteen closure. It seems like we might need to consider a place with kitchen staff to make things easier. @Ryuji, the transport costs and strict terms for whole-building lets are important factors to consider. We need to ensure we have a flexible plan in case of last-minute changes. @Rin, the lottery process and attendance sheets highlight the importance of planning and ensuring everyone's attendance. @Misaki, the first-train times and seniors' views on year-group mixing are crucial for a successful camp. It seems like having everyone stay together might encourage better interaction and bonding.","{""words"":102,""mentions"":[""Shizue"",""Ryuji"",""Rin"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Mio, indeed, having kitchen staff would make things much easier for everyone. @Ryuji, the strict terms for whole-building lets are concerning. We need to ensure we have a backup plan in case someone drops out late. @Rin, the lottery process sounds complex, and the attendance sheets show how important it is to plan ahead. @Misaki, it's great to know that having everyone stay together can encourage better interaction. Maybe we should consider a place where everyone can stay together and has kitchen staff.","{""words"":83,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Ryuji"",""Rin"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
